loaf for Debian
===============

The package operates the system deployment. Its settings are in /etc/loaf and
its data, backups and lock are in /var/lib/loaf. Settings layer in this order,
and later layers override earlier ones:

  1. the packaged defaults, shown with 'loaf docs configuration'
  2. /etc/loaf/config.ini and an optional /etc/loaf/models.ini
  3. a portable deployment's config/config.ini when selected with --project-dir

Root, members of the docker group and the loaf systemd service can operate the
system deployment. Backups in /var/lib/loaf/backup are readable by that group,
so any member can restore them. Restoring settings into /etc/loaf needs root:
'sudo loaf restore --archive PATH'. Restored settings, installers and the
terminal server key stay readable by the docker group. The terminal server key
is /etc/loaf/terminal-server.key.

Start the offline deployment at boot after building or restoring its images:

  sudo systemctl enable --now loaf.service

Read the guides with 'loaf docs' and the manual page with 'man loaf'.
Bash completion for loaf is in /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/loaf and
loads in new shells with the bash-completion package.
Docker Engine 26 or newer and Compose 2.26.1 or newer are required. Debian 12
needs Docker's apt repository for both. The default CUDA 13 Ollama build needs
NVIDIA driver 580 or newer, which NVIDIA's repository provides. The CUDA 12
build, ollama_image = loaf-ollama-cuda12, needs driver 550 or newer, such as
Debian 13's own nvidia-driver package.

Purging the package removes the terminal server key and empty directories.
Backups in /var/lib/loaf/backup and the Docker volumes with models and chats
remain.
